================================================================================
NAME
       schemas - structural contracts for resonance-safe packages, triadic
                 coherence, and RTT-aligned system boundaries

SYNOPSIS
       Schemas define:
           • structural boundaries
           • resonance contracts
           • lineage formats
           • operator compatibility
           • package coherence

DESCRIPTION
       Schemas are the structural contract system of RTT. They define the
       allowed shapes, transitions, and resonance boundaries for triads,
       operators, overlays, and resonance packages.

       A schema is not code. It is a structural declaration:
           “This is what the system expects, allows, and guarantees.”

       Schemas ensure that all triadic action remains:
           • coherent
           • resonance-aligned
           • lineage-safe
           • structurally compatible

       Without schemas, resonance packages drift, patterns misalign, and
       triadic cycles lose coherence.

PURPOSE
       Schemas serve four primary roles:

       1. Boundary Definition
              Establishes what structures may enter or leave a package.

       2. Resonance Contract
              Specifies how resonance-time propagates through operators,
              triads, and higher-order patterns.

       3. Lineage Format
              Defines how triadic history is recorded, stored, and validated.

       4. Coherence Enforcement
              Ensures that all components of a resonance package align with
              RTT structural expectations.

STRUCTURAL BOUNDARIES
       Schemas define the “edges” of a system:
           • what inputs are allowed
           • what outputs must look like
           • what transitions are legal
           • what resonance states are valid

       WRSADC uses schemas to validate boundary crossings.

RESONANCE CONTRACTS
       A resonance contract specifies:
           • how resonance-time flows through a structure
           • how triads propagate effects
           • how overlays modify interpretation
           • how operators interact with RT-space

       Contracts prevent incoherent or unsafe resonance propagation.

PACKAGE COHERENCE
       A resonance package is coherent only if:
           • all components share a schema
           • all operators obey resonance contracts
           • all triads follow structural boundaries
           • all overlays respect schema constraints

       Schemas ensure that packages remain stable across:
           • modules
           • agents
           • dispatch layers
           • educational artifacts
           • simulation cycles

SCHEMA TYPES
       structural-schema
              Defines allowed shapes, transitions, and triad patterns.

       resonance-schema
              Defines resonance-time behavior, propagation rules, and
              coherence constraints.

       lineage-schema
              Defines how triadic history is recorded and validated.

       operator-schema
              Defines operator signatures, compatibility, and RT behavior.

       package-schema
              Defines the structure of a complete resonance package.

USAGE
       Schemas are not executed. They are referenced.

       Example (conceptual):
              schema structural {
                  allowed_patterns = [core, sequential, nested]
                  disallowed = [mutation]
              }

              schema resonance {
                  requires_alignment = true
                  propagation = "triadic"
              }

       WRSADC enforces schemas at dispatch time.

INTERACTION WITH WRSADC
       WRSADC uses schemas to:
           • validate incoming operations
           • enforce resonance contracts
           • ensure triadic structure
           • prevent incoherent transitions

       The Engine assumes schemas are correct; WRSADC verifies them.

INTERACTION WITH TRIADS
       Schemas define:
           • which triadic patterns are allowed
           • how triads may nest or expand
           • how resonance flows through cycles
           • how lineage is recorded

       Triads without schemas risk structural drift.

INTERACTION WITH RESONANCE PACKAGES
       A resonance package must include:
           • a package-schema
           • operator-schemas
           • resonance-schema
           • structural-schema
           • lineage-schema

       Packages missing schemas are considered unsafe.

NOTES
       Schemas are the backbone of coherence in RTT. They ensure that triads,
       operators, overlays, and resonance packages remain aligned with the
       structural expectations of resonance-time.

